is_error":false,"num_turns":33,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've built the L2W network by mapping L2W's inputs onto the inputs the L2 network was trained on, with `W1 = W1_L2·M` and `b1 = b1_L2 + W1_L2·c`. W2, b2, W3 and b3 are bit-identical to the source. The three deliverables are in `work/`, and nothing was fitted.\n\n**Mapping:** the L2 network reads per-lane occupancy. Per-lane E/W through demand in L2W is close to L2's (245 vs 262 veh/h), so I kept that per-lane meaning:\n- E1 ← mean of L2W's two straight lanes, E1 and E2.\n- E2 (left pocket) ← E3.\n- E1u ← mean of E1u and E2u.\n- N/S lanes × 0.93, because L2W's N/S lanes are shorter.\n\n**Pathology fixed:** with 1–2 cars waiting elsewhere and nothing else around, the source holds EW-through green forever; one recorded L2 episode stayed stuck for 30 minutes. I added a term driven by t_green that has no effect at the usual 12 s switch point, so that a held green eventually releases waiting cars.\n\n**Checks:**\n- The network gives the same output as the source on the mapped inputs (max logit difference 1.5e-7).\n- Single-movement probes pick the right phase from every current phase.\n- On frozen lone-car test snapshots, cases never served fell from 44/289 to 0, with a 30 s maximum wait.\n\n**Trainability:** median_max_prob 0.988, share above 0.99 0.48, logit gap 4.6, sat_l1 0.0003, sat_l2 0.125, no dead units. It's slightly more confident than the source on L2 (0.963), which comes from the more congested recorded states, not from the weights.\n\n**Predicted test TTS (veh-h):** low 43.5, nominal 59, high 82. The weak point is high demand: the inherited 12 s greens waste time on yellows and starting up, and the busier E/W left-turn pockets will spill back.","ttft_ms":1119,"type":"result","duration_ms":775390,"uuid":"5f9dd71c-186e-4efb-9f33-f2332f74af06","ttft_stream_ms":922,"time_to_request_ms":84,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":6,"resume_other":0,"process_user_inpu